{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a palladium(II)/chiral phosphoric acid catalyzed three-component reaction of aryldiazoacetates, enamines, and imines. The reaction proceeds through a unique mechanism involving C-N bond cleavage of a Mannich-type intermediate, modification of the resulting amino fragment into an ammonium ylide, and stereoselective reassembly to form chiral alpha-amino-delta-oxo pentanoic acid derivatives with high enantioselectivity and diastereoselectivity.",
